{"_id":"6a2ff6ed2204ffbc59e5a6c5","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"bcODvfBqCUwLVXa8HKOFB","description":"# isnull, isna\n\n`isnull()` and `isna()` are equivalent Pandas methods that return a boolean DataFrame or Series indicating which values are missing (NaN). They are the first step in assessing data completeness. Combined with `.sum()`, they give a count of missing values per column, and with boolean indexing they select rows with missing data.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Working with missing data","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/user_guide/missing_data.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aebb3"},{"type":"official","title":"pandas.isnull","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.isnull.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aebb4"},{"type":"official","title":"pandas.isna","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.isna.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aebb5"},{"type":"article","title":"Handling Missing Values with Pandas","url":"https://towardsdatascience.com/handling-missing-values-with-pandas-b876bf6f008f/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aebb6"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:58:21.024Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/bcODvfBqCUwLVXa8HKOFB.md"}